  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat age-based allowance rule does Shawna use to calculate her father's weekly allowance? Shawna's father is six times as old as Shawna. The allowance is paid weekly.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Shawna be \\(x\\) years old. Her father is \\(6x\\) years old.\n\nIf the weekly allowance is proportional to age—such as \\(\\$1\\) per year of age—then:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Father's allowance}=6x \\text{ dollars per week}.\n\\]\n\nThus, Shawna’s rule is to give her father **six times her own weekly allowance**:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s weekly allowance}=6\\times\\text{Shawna’s weekly allowance}.}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Shawna's father is five times as old as Shawna.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Shawna be \\(x\\) years old. Her father is \\(5x\\) years old.\n\nTherefore, if the allowance is based directly on age, Shawna gives her father **five times her own weekly allowance**:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s weekly allowance}=5\\times\\text{Shawna’s weekly allowance}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Shawna is four times as old as Aliya.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Aliya’s age be \\(a\\). Then:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Shawna's age}=4a\n\\]\n\nand her father’s age is:\n\n\\[\n5(4a)=20a.\n\\]\n\nSo Shawna’s father is **20 times as old as Aliya** and **5 times as old as Shawna**.\n\nTherefore, if the weekly allowance is proportional to age, the rule is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s allowance}=5\\times\\text{Shawna’s allowance}\n=20\\times\\text{Aliya’s allowance}.}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Shawna is three times as old as Aliya.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Aliya be \\(a\\) years old.\n\nShawna is three times as old:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Shawna's age}=3a\n\\]\n\nHer father is five times as old as Shawna:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Father's age}=5(3a)=15a\n\\]\n\nThus, the allowance rule is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s weekly allowance}=5\\times\\text{Shawna’s allowance}\n=15\\times\\text{Aliya’s allowance}.}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Aliya is 3 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old.\n\nShawna is three times as old:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 3=9\n\\]\n\nShawna’s father is five times as old as Shawna:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 9=45\n\\]\n\nSo the ages are:\n\n- Aliya: \\(3\\)\n- Shawna: \\(9\\)\n- Father: \\(45\\)\n\nTherefore, the age-based allowance rule is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Father’s weekly allowance}=45\\text{ dollars, if the rule is \\$1 per year of age}.}\n\\]\n\nEquivalently, he receives five times Shawna’s allowance and fifteen times Aliya’s allowance.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Shawna gives her father an allowance equal to 2 dollars for each year of his age.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Shawna’s father is \\(45\\) years old.\n\nShe gives him \\(\\$2\\) for each year of his age:\n\n\\[\n45 \\times \\$2=\\$90\n\\]\n\nTherefore, his weekly allowance is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$90\\text{ per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How old is Shawna's father?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old.\n\nShawna is three times Aliya’s age:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 3=9\n\\]\n\nHer father is five times Shawna’s age:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 9=45\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{Shawna’s father is 45 years old.}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
